Sessions are stored as append-only JSONL files under ~/.rho/sessions/: ~/.rho/sessions/ └── <project-hash>/ └── <unix-timestamp>_<session-id>.jsonl Project hash : first 16 hex characters of SHA-256 of the canonical project root path. This groups sessions by project. Auto-flush : every append writes to disk immediately. A crash loses at most the last entry. Format : each line is a JSON object with a type discriminator (Header or Entry). The first line is always a Header with session metadata. Example JSONL file: {"type":"Header","id":"4b021d5d","version":1,"created_at_secs":1777859536,"cwd":"/home/user/project","parent_session":null}
{"type":"Entry","id":"a1b2c3d4","parent_id":null,"timestamp":{...},"resolution":"Full","payload":{"Message":{"content":"you are a coding assistant","role":"system"}}}
{"type":"Entry","id":"e5f6a7b8","parent_id":"a1b2c3d4","timestamp":{...},"resolution":"Full","payload":{"Message":{"content":"fix the bug","role":"user"}}}

